{
  "id": "folding_range/line_folding/07_collapsed_lines",
  "topic": "folding_range",
  "subtopic": "line_folding",
  "title": "Closing lines fold in",
  "summary": "A client that shows collapsed text folds a block's closing line too, `int area(Point p) {...}`",
  "prose": "Each fold shows its first line followed by `...`; when the closing brace,\n`#endif` or `*/` sits on a line of its own, that line folds in and shows\nafter the `...`. A closing line that opens the next block, such as\n`} else {`, stays visible.\n\n> **Client support**: Neovim shows the text through `vim.lsp.foldtext()`.\n> VS Code shows no collapsed text, so the closing line stays visible there\n> ([vscode#3352](https://github.com/microsoft/vscode/issues/3352)).",
  "status": "supported",
  "issues": [],
  "files": [
    {
      "path": "main.cpp",
      "text": "namespace shapes\n{\n\nstruct Point {\n    int x;\n    int y;\n};\n\nint area(Point p) {\n    if (p.x > 0) {\n        return p.x * p.y;\n    } else {\n        return 0;\n    }\n}\n\nint scaled(Point p,\n           int factor)\n{\n    return area(p) * factor;\n}\n\n}  // namespace shapes\n\n/*\n * Debug helpers.\n */\n#ifdef SHAPES_DEBUG\nvoid dump();\n#endif\n\nvoid visit(void (*callback)(int));\n\nvoid run() {\n    visit([](int value) {\n        value += 1;\n    });\n}\n",
      "markers": []
    }
  ],
